</section>
</section>
<section class="ltx_appendix" id="A2">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix">
<span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Additional Experimental Details</h2>
<section class="ltx_paragraph" id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Training and Inference using Align4Gen.</h4>
<div class="ltx_para" id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1">
<p class="ltx_p">For patch token alignment, a single MLP is employed to map all patches, rather than using separate MLPs for each patch. This ensures a consistent mapping across patches through a shared MLP. Additionally, when performing concatenation, the feature vectors should first be normalized along the feature dimension before concatenation. This normalization step is crucial because the projection loss is computed using cosine similarity. Without normalization, discrepancies in the scale of the feature vectors could cause one feature to dominate the other, thereby diminishing its influence. By normalizing both feature vectors before concatenation, we ensure a balanced alignment. During training, this alignment process is applied, while at inference, the MLP is removed, and the video diffusion model is used as in standard inference.</p>
</div>
<figure class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top" id="alg1">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 1</span> </span> Training Procedure</figcaption>
<div class="ltx_listing ltx_listing">
<div class="ltx_listingline" id="alg1.l1">
<span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">1:</span>Video <math alttext="\mathcal{V}" class="ltx_Math" display="inline" id="alg1.l1.m1"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}</annotation></semantics></math>, VAE <math alttext="\mathcal{E}_{\text{VAE}}" class="ltx_Math" display="inline" id="alg1.l1.m2"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mtext>VAE</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{\text{VAE}}</annotation></semantics></math>, DINOv2 <math alttext="\mathcal{E}_{\text{DINOv2}}" class="ltx_Math" display="inline" id="alg1.l1.m3"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mtext>DINOv2</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{\text{DINOv2}}</annotation></semantics></math>, SAM2.1 Hiera <math alttext="\mathcal{E}_{\text{SAM}}" class="ltx_Math" display="inline" id="alg1.l1.m4"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mtext>SAM</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{\text{SAM}}</annotation></semantics></math>, trainable <math alttext="MLP(\cdot)" class="ltx_Math" display="inline" id="alg1.l1.m5"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">MLP(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math alttext="\gamma" class="ltx_Math" display="inline" id="alg1.l1.m6"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div class="ltx_listingline" id="alg1.l2">
<span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">2:</span>Total Loss <math alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\text{total}}" class="ltx_Math" display="inline" id="alg1.l2.m1"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>total</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\text{total}}</annotation></semantics></math>
</div>
<div class="ltx_listingline" id="alg1.l3">
<span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">3:</span><span class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">// Step 1: Encode video using VAE</span>
</div>
<div class="ltx_listingline" id="alg1.l4">
<span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">4:</span><math alttext="\mathbf{z}\leftarrow\mathcal{E}_{\text{VAE}}(\mathcal{V})" class="ltx_Math" display="inline" id="alg1.l4.m1"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐳</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mtext>VAE</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{z}\leftarrow\mathcal{E}_{\text{VAE}}(\mathcal{V})</annotation></semantics></math> <span class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math alttext="\triangleright" class="ltx_Math" display="inline" id="alg1.l4.m2"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> Encode the video <math alttext="\mathcal{V}" class="ltx_Math" display="inline" id="alg1.l4.m3"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}</annotation></semantics></math>
</span>
</div>
<div class="ltx_listingline" id="alg1.l5">
<span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">5:</span><span class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">// Step 2: Extract features using Vision Encoders</span>
</div>
<div class="ltx_listingline" id="alg1.l6">
<span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">6:</span><math alttext="F_{1}\leftarrow\mathcal{E}_{\text{DINOv2}}(\mathcal{V})" class="ltx_Math" display="inline" id="alg1.l6.m1"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mtext>DINOv2</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{1}\leftarrow\mathcal{E}_{\text{DINOv2}}(\mathcal{V})</annotation></semantics></math> <span class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math alttext="\triangleright" class="ltx_Math" display="inline" id="alg1.l6.m2"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> Extract feature <math alttext="F_{1}" class="ltx_Math" display="inline" id="alg1.l6.m3"><semantics><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> using <math alttext="\mathcal{E}_{\text{DINOv2}}" class="ltx_Math" display="inline" id="alg1.l6.m4"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mtext>DINOv2</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{\text{DINOv2}}</annotation></semantics></math>
</span>
</div>
<div class="ltx_listingline" id="alg1.l7">
<span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">7:</span><math alttext="F_{2}\leftarrow\mathcal{E}_{\text{SAM}}(\mathcal{V})" class="ltx_Math" display="inline" id="alg1.l7.m1"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mtext>SAM</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{2}\leftarrow\mathcal{E}_{\text{SAM}}(\mathcal{V})</annotation></semantics></math> <span class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math alttext="\triangleright" class="ltx_Math" display="inline" id="alg1.l7.m2"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> Extract feature <math alttext="F_{2}" class="ltx_Math" display="inline" id="alg1.l7.m3"><semantics><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> using <math alttext="\mathcal{E}_{\text{SAM}}" class="ltx_Math" display="inline" id="alg1.l7.m4"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mtext>SAM</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{\text{SAM}}</annotation></semantics></math>
</span>
</div>
<div class="ltx_listingline" id="alg1.l8">
<span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">8:</span><span class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">// Step 3: Normalize and concatenate features</span>
</div>
<div class="ltx_listingline" id="alg1.l9">
<span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">9:</span><math alttext="F\leftarrow\Bigl{[}\frac{F_{1}}{\|F_{1}\|};\ \frac{F_{2}}{\|F_{2}\|}\Bigr{]}" class="ltx_Math" display="inline" id="alg1.l9.m1"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo rspace="0.667em">;</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F\leftarrow\Bigl{[}\frac{F_{1}}{\|F_{1}\|};\ \frac{F_{2}}{\|F_{2}\|}\Bigr{]}</annotation></semantics></math> <span class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math alttext="\triangleright" class="ltx_Math" display="inline" id="alg1.l9.m2"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> Feature Fusion
</span>
</div>
<div class="ltx_listingline" id="alg1.l10">
<span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">10:</span><span class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">// Step 4: Compute Projection Loss</span>
</div>
<div class="ltx_listingline" id="alg1.l11">
<span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">11:</span><math alttext="f\leftarrow MLP(\text{intermediate diffusion feature})" class="ltx_Math" display="inline" id="alg1.l11.m1"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext>intermediate diffusion feature</mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f\leftarrow MLP(\text{intermediate diffusion feature})</annotation></semantics></math>
</div>
<div class="ltx_listingline" id="alg1.l12">
<span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">12:</span><math alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\text{proj}}\leftarrow 1-\cos\bigl{(}f,\,F\bigr{)}" class="ltx_Math" display="inline" id="alg1.l12.m1"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>proj</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mi>F</mi><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\text{proj}}\leftarrow 1-\cos\bigl{(}f,\,F\bigr{)}</annotation></semantics></math>
</div>
<div class="ltx_listingline" id="alg1.l13">
<span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">13:</span><span class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">// Step 5: Calculate Total Loss</span>
</div>
<div class="ltx_listingline" id="alg1.l14">
<span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">14:</span><math alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\text{total}}\leftarrow\mathcal{L}_{\text{diffusion}}+\gamma\,\mathcal{L}_{\text{proj}}" class="ltx_Math" display="inline" id="alg1.l14.m1"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>total</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>diffusion</mtext></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>proj</mtext></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\text{total}}\leftarrow\mathcal{L}_{\text{diffusion}}+\gamma\,\mathcal{L}_{\text{proj}}</annotation></semantics></math>
</div>
<div class="ltx_listingline" id="alg1.l15">
<span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">15:</span><span class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">return</span> <math alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\text{total}}" class="ltx_Math" display="inline" id="alg1.l15.m1"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>total</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\text{total}}</annotation></semantics></math>
</div>
</div>
</figure>
<figure class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top" id="alg2">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 2</span> </span> Inference Procedure</figcaption>
<div class="ltx_listing ltx_listing">
<div class="ltx_listingline" id="alg2.l1">
<span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">1:</span>Flow model <math alttext="f(\mathbf{z},t)" class="ltx_Math" display="inline" id="alg2.l1.m1"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(\mathbf{z},t)</annotation></semantics></math>, initial latent <math alttext="\mathbf{z}_{T}" class="ltx_Math" display="inline" id="alg2.l1.m2"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{z}_{T}</annotation></semantics></math>, VAE Decoder <math alttext="\mathcal{D}_{\text{VAE}}" class="ltx_Math" display="inline" id="alg2.l1.m3"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mtext>VAE</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{\text{VAE}}</annotation></semantics></math>, total time <math alttext="T" class="ltx_Math" display="inline" id="alg2.l1.m4"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math>, and time step <math alttext="\Delta t" class="ltx_Math" display="inline" id="alg2.l1.m5"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta t</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div class="ltx_listingline" id="alg2.l2">
<span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">2:</span>Generated video <math alttext="\hat{\mathcal{V}}" class="ltx_Math" display="inline" id="alg2.l2.m1"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mathcal{V}}</annotation></semantics></math>
</div>
<div class="ltx_listingline" id="alg2.l3">
<span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">3:</span><span class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">// Step 1: Initialization</span>
</div>
<div class="ltx_listingline" id="alg2.l4">
<span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">4:</span><math alttext="t\leftarrow T" class="ltx_Math" display="inline" id="alg2.l4.m1"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\leftarrow T</annotation></semantics></math>
</div>
<div class="ltx_listingline" id="alg2.l5">
<span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">5:</span><math alttext="\mathbf{z}\leftarrow\mathbf{z}_{T}" class="ltx_Math" display="inline" id="alg2.l5.m1"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐳</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>T</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{z}\leftarrow\mathbf{z}_{T}</annotation></semantics></math> <span class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math alttext="\triangleright" class="ltx_Math" display="inline" id="alg2.l5.m2"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> Initialized from <math alttext="N(0,I)" class="ltx_Math" display="inline" id="alg2.l5.m3"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N(0,I)</annotation></semantics></math>
</span>
</div>
<div class="ltx_listingline" id="alg2.l6">
<span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">6:</span><span class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">// Step 2: Euler Integration for Flow Model</span>
</div>
<div class="ltx_listingline" id="alg2.l7">
<span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">7:</span><span class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">while</span> <math alttext="t&gt;0" class="ltx_Math" display="inline" id="alg2.l7.m1"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> <span class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>
</div>
<div class="ltx_listingline" id="alg2.l8">
<span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">8:</span>  <math alttext="\mathbf{z}\leftarrow\mathbf{z}+f(\mathbf{z},t)\,\Delta t" class="ltx_Math" display="inline" id="alg2.l8.m1"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐳</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{z}\leftarrow\mathbf{z}+f(\mathbf{z},t)\,\Delta t</annotation></semantics></math>
</div>
<div class="ltx_listingline" id="alg2.l9">
<span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">9:</span>  <math alttext="t\leftarrow t-\Delta t" class="ltx_Math" display="inline" id="alg2.l9.m1"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\leftarrow t-\Delta t</annotation></semantics></math>
</div>
<div class="ltx_listingline" id="alg2.l10">
<span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">10:</span><span class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">while</span>
</div>
<div class="ltx_listingline" id="alg2.l11">
<span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">11:</span><span class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">// Step 3: Decode the Final Latent to Generate Video</span>
</div>
<div class="ltx_listingline" id="alg2.l12">
<span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">12:</span><math alttext="\hat{\mathcal{V}}\leftarrow\mathcal{D}_{\text{VAE}}(\mathbf{z})" class="ltx_Math" display="inline" id="alg2.l12.m1"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mtext>VAE</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐳</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mathcal{V}}\leftarrow\mathcal{D}_{\text{VAE}}(\mathbf{z})</annotation></semantics></math>
</div>
<div class="ltx_listingline" id="alg2.l13">
<span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">13:</span><span class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">return</span> <math alttext="\hat{\mathcal{V}}" class="ltx_Math" display="inline" id="alg2.l13.m1"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mathcal{V}}</annotation></semantics></math>
</div>
</div>
</figure>
</section>
<section class="ltx_paragraph" id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Datasets.</h4>
<div class="ltx_para" id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1">
<p class="ltx_p">We validate our experiments using three video datasets: one class-conditional dataset and two unconditional datasets.</p>
</div>
<div class="ltx_para ltx_noindent" id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2">
<p class="ltx_p"><span class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">UCF-101.</span>
UCF-101 <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(Soomro, Zamir, and Shah <a class="ltx_ref" href="https://arxiv.org/html/2509.09547v1#bib.bib42" title="">2012</a>)</cite> is a widely used action recognition dataset that contains 13,320 videos spanning 101 action categories. For our experiments, we use only the training split for model training, ensuring that the test split is not utilized during training. All metric evaluations are conducted on the test split.</p>
</div>
<div class="ltx_para ltx_noindent" id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p3">
<p class="ltx_p"><span class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">SkyTimelapse.</span> SkyTimelapse is an unconstrained video dataset featuring various time-lapse sequences of the sky, capturing dynamic weather changes and atmospheric conditions. As in  <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(Yu et al. <a class="ltx_ref" href="https://arxiv.org/html/2509.09547v1#bib.bib56" title="">2023</a>)</cite>, we conduct both training and evaluation on the training split.</p>
</div>
<div class="ltx_para ltx_noindent" id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p4">
<p class="ltx_p"><span class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">FaceForensics.</span>
FaceForensics <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(Rössler et al. <a class="ltx_ref" href="https://arxiv.org/html/2509.09547v1#bib.bib36" title="">2019</a>)</cite> is a dataset designed for facial manipulation detection, containing both real and manipulated face videos. We follow the same protocol as SkyTimeLapse, using the training split for both model training and metric evaluations.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section class="ltx_appendix" id="A3">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix">
<span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>V-DiT Architecture</h2>
<figure class="ltx_figure" id="A3.F7"><img alt="Refer to caption" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_square" height="662" id="A3.F7.g1" src="figs/suppl_dit.png" width="598"/>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 7: </span>(a) The V-DiT architecture, consisting of <math alttext="N" class="ltx_Math" display="inline" id="A3.F7.m2"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> transformer blocks, each comprising one spatial block and one temporal block. (b) The architecture of a single transformer block.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div class="ltx_para" id="A3.p1">
<p class="ltx_p">V-DiT constructs the latent space representation of a video by processing frames individually using the VAE from Stable Diffusion v1.4 <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(Rombach et al. <a class="ltx_ref" href="https://arxiv.org/html/2509.09547v1#bib.bib34" title="">2022</a>)</cite>. Each frame is then transformed into patches via patch embedding, specifically employing a uniform frame patch embedding strategy, where patches are extracted in a frame-wise manner without inter-frame interactions.</p>
</div>
<div class="ltx_para" id="A3.p2">
<p class="ltx_p">The model consists of <math alttext="N" class="ltx_Math" display="inline" id="A3.p2.m1"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> transformer blocks, where each unit comprises two sub-blocks: a spatial transformer block and a temporal transformer block. The architecture stacks these units iteratively to build the full transformer model. To encode positional information, spatial positional embeddings and temporal positional embeddings are incorporated before the input is passed into the transformer blocks. Notably, the temporal positional embeddings are applied after the first spatial transformer block and before entering the first temporal transformer block.</p>
</div>
<div class="ltx_para" id="A3.p3">
<p class="ltx_p">Additionally, to incorporate timestep and class information, the model employs adaptive layer normalization (AdaLN), where the scaling parameters <math alttext="\beta" class="ltx_Math" display="inline" id="A3.p3.m1"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> and <math alttext="\gamma" class="ltx_Math" display="inline" id="A3.p3.m2"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math> are learned through a linear projection of the timestep and class embeddings.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section class="ltx_appendix" id="A4">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix">
<span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>Additional Feature Analysis</h2>
<section class="ltx_subsection" id="A4.SSx1">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection">Additional Assessment of Temporal Stability</h3>
<div class="ltx_para" id="A4.SSx1.p1">
<p class="ltx_p">Video encoders such as VideoMAE, which are trained with objectives like masked frame reconstruction and temporal modeling, primarily capture semantic-level dynamics for tasks such as action recognition by aggregating multiple frames into spatio-temporal patches.
While effective for classification, this design often results in lower discriminability and reduced temporal stability, as also reported in recent zero-shot video segmentation studies <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(Wang et al. <a class="ltx_ref" href="https://arxiv.org/html/2509.09547v1#bib.bib48" title="">2025</a>)</cite>.
Such instability poses challenges for feature alignment in video diffusion models, where a shared MLP projects all tokens regardless of their temporal position.
In particular, fluctuations in object features across frames can make the alignment optimization process unstable.</p>
</div>
<div class="ltx_para" id="A4.SSx1.p2">
<p class="ltx_p">In contrast, image encoders such as DINOv2 and SAM2 better preserve local patterns and maintain consistent spatial representations when applied frame-by-frame, leading to more stable alignment.
Moreover, PCA-based color consistency serves as a qualitative indicator of temporal coherence; for example, frame-to-frame color shifts can introduce tracking errors (see Fig. <a class="ltx_ref" href="https://arxiv.org/html/2509.09547v1#A1.F6" title="Figure 6 ‣ Frame-wise CLIP similarity. ‣ Appendix A Evaluation Metrics ‣ Improving Video Diffusion Transformer Training by Multi-Feature Fusion and Alignment from Self-Supervised Vision Encoders"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>).
Such color-consistency analysis has also been adopted as a practical proxy for evaluating temporal stability in prior works, including TokenFlow <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(Geyer et al. <a class="ltx_ref" href="https://arxiv.org/html/2509.09547v1#bib.bib11" title="">2023</a>)</cite> and Chrono PointTrack <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(Kim et al. <a class="ltx_ref" href="https://arxiv.org/html/2509.09547v1#bib.bib20" title="">2025</a>)</cite>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section class="ltx_subsection" id="A4.SSx2">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection">Analysis of Generative Model Feature Representation (SD3)</h3>
<figure class="ltx_figure" id="A4.F8"><img alt="Refer to caption" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_square" height="494" id="A4.F8.g1" src="figs/pca_sd3.png" width="598"/>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 8: </span>Based on our PCA analysis of the SD3 transformer block, we observed that the output following the 22th transformer block is the most discriminative and retains high-frequency details. Therefore, we have decided to use this feature for alignment.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div class="ltx_para" id="A4.SSx2.p1">
<p class="ltx_p">We conducted a PCA analysis of features extracted from the transformer blocks of SD3 at different layer depths. The results showed that as the layer depth increased, the extracted information became more detailed and well-defined. Based on the PCA results in Fig. <a class="ltx_ref" href="https://arxiv.org/html/2509.09547v1#A4.F8" title="Figure 8 ‣ Analysis of Generative Model Feature Representation (SD3) ‣ Appendix D Additional Feature Analysis ‣ Improving Video Diffusion Transformer Training by Multi-Feature Fusion and Alignment from Self-Supervised Vision Encoders"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>, we identified that the output features from the 22th transformer block exhibited the highest degree of object distinction and consistency. Therefore, we selected the features from this specific layer in Tab <a class="ltx_ref" href="https://arxiv.org/html/2509.09547v1#S4.T4" title="Table 4 ‣ Effect of feature alignment layer. ‣ Ablation Studies ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ Improving Video Diffusion Transformer Training by Multi-Feature Fusion and Alignment from Self-Supervised Vision Encoders"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<figure class="ltx_figure" id="A4.F9">
