</tbody>
</table>
</span></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 7: </span>FVD comparison of different methods.
We report standard I3D-based FVD without content-debiased evaluation.</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
</section>
<section class="ltx_appendix" id="A6">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix">
<span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix F </span>Comparison to Previous Methods</h2>
<div class="ltx_para" id="A6.p1">
<p class="ltx_p">To rigorously validate the effectiveness of our method, it is ideal to conduct training under identical conditions (e.g., batch size, learning rate, etc.). However, prior works adopt varying batch sizes and learning rates, making a direct comparison inherently challenging. For fairness, we nonetheless report Fréchet Video Distance (FVD) values for all methods. Specifically, for Latte, we re-trained the model using our experimental settings; for PVDM, we used the publicly released checkpoint; and for Matten, which is not publicly available, we report the values provided in its original paper. Moreover, since none of the compared methods employed content-debiased FVD, we evaluate all methods using the standard I3D-based FVD metric. Our approach not only enhances the original baseline but also achieves superior performance compared to all other baselines as Tab <a class="ltx_ref" href="https://arxiv.org/html/2509.09547v1#A5.T7" title="Table 7 ‣ Extending Text-to-Image to Text-to-Video. ‣ Appendix E Limitation ‣ Improving Video Diffusion Transformer Training by Multi-Feature Fusion and Alignment from Self-Supervised Vision Encoders"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section class="ltx_appendix" id="A7">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix">
<span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix G </span>Additional Qualitative Results</h2>
<div class="ltx_para" id="A7.p1">
<p class="ltx_p">We provide additional qualitative comparison results in Fig. <a class="ltx_ref" href="https://arxiv.org/html/2509.09547v1#A7.F10" title="Figure 10 ‣ Appendix G Additional Qualitative Results ‣ Improving Video Diffusion Transformer Training by Multi-Feature Fusion and Alignment from Self-Supervised Vision Encoders"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a>, <a class="ltx_ref" href="https://arxiv.org/html/2509.09547v1#A7.F13" title="Figure 13 ‣ Appendix G Additional Qualitative Results ‣ Improving Video Diffusion Transformer Training by Multi-Feature Fusion and Alignment from Self-Supervised Vision Encoders"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">13</span></a>, and <a class="ltx_ref" href="https://arxiv.org/html/2509.09547v1#A7.F14" title="Figure 14 ‣ Appendix G Additional Qualitative Results ‣ Improving Video Diffusion Transformer Training by Multi-Feature Fusion and Alignment from Self-Supervised Vision Encoders"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">14</span></a>. Please visit our project page for full video results.</p>
</div>
